## Next action to discuss

1. Trace the H2 age-group difference in before-to-after changes, its uncertainty, and the detectable-effect calculation.

2. Trace the H2b before- and after-move level comparisons and the exact all-controls specification.

3. Check how the H2b result changes across instruments and control sets, including the reported role of market value.

4. Verify the coverage-volume denominators, model specifications, and ratio interpretation.

5. Check how reported intervals and permutation p-values are constructed, including label shuffling with controls, so statistical labels match the implemented procedure.

6. Retain the distinction between a change with substantial uncertainty and evidence of equivalence. Record when H2b emerged and which decisions followed exploration.

